<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47936" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tertĭārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>containing a third part.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stannum,</span>”
				<i>that contains one part of white and two of black
					lead</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					34, 17, 48, § 160</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tertĭārĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n., <i>a third part</i>,
				<i>a third</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
				95, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4, 7, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
